---
/**
 * The one line at the foot of a documentation page that tells a reader this page has a
 * machine-readable form, and where the whole set of them is.
 *
 * WHY IT EXISTS AT ALL. `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt` and the `.md` twins were all reachable and
 * none of them was announced: three surfaces built for machines, discoverable only by someone who
 * already guessed they were there. A person pasting a docs page into a chat gets a page of portal
 * chrome; the same person one line lower gets the prose.
 *
 * WHY IT IS A LINE AND NOT A CARD. Placement was the whole decision. This is a footer note, under
 * the pagination, in the muted colour the last-updated line already uses, because it is a fact ABOUT
 * the page rather than part of it. A bordered box or a button would put a developer affordance in
 * front of every reader who came to find out why their backup failed, and rank it above the
 * documentation on its own page. Nothing new is invented visually: the glyph is `Icon`, the type
 * scale is `--bo-t-13`, the colour is `--bo-muted`, the same token the portal's other footer-weight lines use, and the underline
 * behaviour is the one the prose links use.
 *
 * DOCUMENTATION ONLY. `DocsFooter` renders this under the same condition it renders the rating
 * block: not on the splash landing, not on `/contact`, `/roadmap` or `/requests`. Those three are
 * `.astro` pages rendered through `StarlightPage` and have no entry in the docs collection, so they
 * have no `.md` twin either; a link to one would 404, which is the defect this app shipped last
 * (a dead `/chat` in the sidebar, 404 on all 41 pages, every gate green).
 */
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import { idToMdPath } from '../lib/docs-index';

interface Props {
  /** Collection id of the page this footer belongs to, e.g. `backups/reading-a-run`. */
  id: string;
}

const { id } = Astro.props;
const mdPath = idToMdPath(id);
---

<p class="ds-line not-content" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <Icon name="file-text" size={14} />
  <span>
    For AI and scripts: <a href={mdPath}>this page as Markdown</a>, an <a href="/llms.txt"
      >index of every page</a
    >, or <a href="/llms-full.txt">the whole documentation in one file</a>.
  </span>
</p>

<style>
  /* Sits under Starlight's own footer, which ends with the last-updated line and the pagination
     pair. 24px is the gap the pagination already keeps below itself, so this reads as one more
     line of the same block rather than as a new section. */
  .ds-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-13);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* The glyph inherits `currentColor` from the line, so it is muted with the text rather than
     coloured separately. The nudge keeps it on the first line's optical baseline: `align-items:
     flex-start` puts its box top at the line box top, which sits it about 2px high against
     lower-case text. Optical, not grid, which is the one case the 4px rule exempts. */
  .ds-line :global(.bo-i) {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .ds-line a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    transition: color 150ms ease-out;
  }

  .ds-line a:hover {
    color: var(--bo-primary);
  }
</style>
